From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Łukasz Buśko <lukasz.busko@guns4hire.cc>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 07:27:39 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: mediatek: mt7988a-bpi-r4-pro: add SerDes mux for LAN

The 10G LAN SerDes of the BPi-R4 Pro 8X reaches either the external
Aeonsemi AS21010 PHY (phy24) or the SFP1 cage through a passive mux
driven by the SFP1 module detect line. Describe both lanes as channels
of a "mxl862xx,ds-mux" attached to switch port 13 so the lane is
selected at runtime instead of by a boot-time overlay.

Like the WAN side, the mux node does not repeat the module detect GPIO
of the cage and asks the SFP bus of its SFP channel for the module
presence instead.

The port node itself describes the PHY lane, which is the state the mux
starts in, and port 13 is enabled as lan6. Channel ids match the
logical chan-sel GPIO value: channel 0 is the SFP lane, channel 1 the
PHY lane. The channels need no pcs-handle because the SerDes PCS of a
switch port is picked by the switch driver in mac_select_pcs().

Like the WAN side, the PHY lane uses USXGMII with in-band status and the
SFP lane keeps fixed-rate 10GBASE-R: the PHY rate-adapts the SerDes to
the copper speed, which the switch PCS only follows with USXGMII
negotiation enabled, while a 10G SFP+ module has no USXGMII AN to
complete.

Based on the Bananapi BPi-R4 Pro 8X vendor device tree.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt7988a-bananapi-bpi-r4-pro-8x.dts | 36 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 35 insertions, 1 deletion

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt7988a-bananapi-bpi-r4-pro-8x.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt7988a-bananapi-bpi-r4-pro-8x.dts
@@ -59,11 +59,45 @@
 };
 
 &switch16 {
+	ds_mux: ds-mux-bus {
+		#address-cells = <1>;
+		#size-cells = <0>;
+
+		ds_mux0: ds-mux@13 {
+			compatible = "mxl862xx,ds-mux";
+			reg = <13>;
+			#address-cells = <1>;
+			#size-cells = <0>;
+			chan-sel-gpios = <&pio 54 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+			sfp-present-channel = <0>;
+
+			ds_mux0_sfp: channel@0 {
+				reg = <0>;
+				phy-mode = "10gbase-r";
+				phy-connection-type = "10gbase-r";
+				managed = "in-band-status";
+				sfp = <&sfp1>;
+			};
+
+			ds_mux0_phy: channel@1 {
+				reg = <1>;
+				phy-mode = "usxgmii";
+				phy-connection-type = "usxgmii";
+				managed = "in-band-status";
+				phy-handle = <&phy24>;
+			};
+		};
+	};
+
 	ports {
 		port@13 {
 			reg = <13>;
 			label = "lan6";
-			status = "disabled";
+			phy-handle = <&phy24>;
+			phy-mode = "usxgmii";
+			phy-connection-type = "usxgmii";
+			managed = "in-band-status";
+			status = "okay";
 		};
 	};
 };
